<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/10th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Capture of Awdaghast (992)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/992">992 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/awdaghast">Awdaghast</a> in 992 CE was the conquest by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana-empire">Ghana Empire</a> of the oasis town of Awdaghast, previously held by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zanata-berbers">Zanata Berbers</a>. The town lay at the southern Saharan end of a major <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gold-trade">trans-Saharan gold</a> route. The site describes the conquest as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a>'s most significant offensive military achievement, giving it direct control over key points of the gold trade.</p></div>
